# CLAUDE.md.example
# Copy to CLAUDE.md (gitignored) and adapt. Keep it under ~100 lines.

## Project
usb-android-tethering: a userspace Rust driver that exposes an Android phone's USB
tethering (RNDIS, CDC-NCM, CDC-ECM) to macOS as a real Ethernet adapter. Read
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, especially the Invariants section, before touching teardown
order, USB transfer ownership or the network-service lifecycle.

## Commands
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo clippy --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --locked
cargo build --release
sudo ./target/release/usb-android-tethering -vv   # hardware run, Ctrl+C restores

## Rules
- The data path must not allocate per packet or wake on a timer while idle.
- Parsing runs on device-controlled bytes: bounds-check, never panic.
- Unsafe is only for FFI; each block says why it is sound.
- Do not run adb as root. Do not detach a native macOS driver.
